1. **`update_subscription` (PATCH) — CWE-639 IDOR**: The endpoint at line 83 accepts an `email` query parameter and performs subscription operations (cancel/resubscribe) for any Stripe customer matching that email. It only checks `@requires(["authenticated"])` but never verifies that `request.user` matches the supplied `email` parameter. Any authenticated user can cancel or resubscribe another user's subscription.

2. **`subscribe` (POST webhook) — CWE-862**: The POST webhook at line 23-78 has no authentication decorator. It does call `stripe.Webhook.construct_event` to verify the Stripe signature, which is a valid webhook authentication mechanism. This is intentional (webhooks come from Stripe, not users), so this is not a flaw per se — but it relies entirely on `endpoint_secret` being set and the signature check not being bypassable.

